he length-check from step 2 and its Acceptance Criterion; if a gap is believed to remain, name what the two existing guards fail to catch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Drop the new 'effective characters' length check (the length invariant is already enforced in UTF-8 bytes by tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py) or, if a length assertion is wanted alongside the drift check, measure UTF-8 bytes to match the provider limit — do not re-assert the same limit in a weaker character unit.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'and when a heredoc description exceeds 1,024 effective characters'","tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py:15 `_ALARM_DESCRIPTION_BYTE_LIMIT = 1024`","tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py:36-37 `return len(self.value.encode(\"utf-8\"))`","tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py:145-147 'AWS validates alarm_description in UTF-8 bytes, not Python characters; limit